  "verbalization": "The compound [(3R,4S,5S)-4-(hydroxymethyl)-5-(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)oxolan-3-yl]-(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)methanone is linked to the CD70 antigen through a series of molecular interactions. It is identified as a target of Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including Spruceanol and Capensinidin. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of CD70 antigen expression, suggesting a potential role for the compound in modulating CD70 antigen activity. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, which is a known target of CD70 antigen. This connection implies that the compound could influence CD70 antigen function through a mechanism involving the vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, potentially through a regulatory pathway that involves metabolic or signaling processes. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for the compound in the regulation of CD70 antigen, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
